    "overview": {
      "body": "A windtrap is desert infrastructure in the most literal sense. It stands between a colony and slow dehydration by harvesting the world the colony was dropped into instead of waiting for rescue from it."
    },
    "settlementRole": {
      "body": "Once established, a windtrap changes the rhythm of the campaign. Travel, labor planning, and storage still matter, but the settlement is no longer surviving on carried reserves alone."
    },
    "siting": {
      "body": "Placement matters. The machine works best when the player gives it air and room, which turns water production into a map-reading problem instead of a flat production stat."
    },
